  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the healthcare needs of medical evacuees in Egypt in response to Gaza crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support and strengthen the Egyptian healthcare system to address the urgent medical needs of individuals suffering from acute and war-related injuries, such as trauma, burns, and complex surgical conditions, as well as the needs of patients with renal failure, and cancer, which have been worsened by prolonged disruptions in healthcare access within Gaza.

This will be achieved through 1- Ensuring the availability of medical consumables, equipment, and medications to effectively manage and treat the expected range of conditions among the medical evacuees.
2- Enhancing the capacities of HCWs within the healthcare facilities, receiving medical evacuees, in emergency and critical care. 
3- Improving access of medical evacuees to quality healthcare services</narrative>
  </description>
